[[File:The Mountain.png|right|500px]]
'''The Mountain''' is an exterior region in the northern part of Stardew Valley. Initially, there are only two exits: to the south leading to [[Pelican Town]], and to the west leading to the [[Backwoods]]. However, over the course of the game, several events open up new routes:
* On [[Spring]] 5, debris blocking the bridge north of the lake is cleared, providing access to [[the Mines]] and the [[Adventurer's Guild]].
* On [[Summer]] 3, an earthquake opens a pass north from the Mountain to the [[Railroad]].
* The bridge leading to the [[Quarry]] at the east end of the map can be repaired (by completing all [[Bundles#Crafts Room|Crafts Room Bundles]] or purchasing "Bridge" from the [[Joja Community Development Form]] for {{Price|25000}}).
* The Glittering Boulder blocking the water flow west of the mine entrance can be removed (by completing all [[Bundles#Fish Tank|Fish Tank Bundles]] or purchasing "Panning" from the Joja Community Development Form for {{Price|20000}}).
* After completing the [[Community Center]] or purchasing the [[JojaMart]] subscription for {{Price|5000}} you can purchase a "[[Carpenter's Shop#Community Upgrades|Community Upgrade]]" which will upgrade the [[trailer]] and open up some hidden passages. One will be located south of the [[Adventurer's Guild]] and will lead to the river waterfall north of [[JojaMart]].
